    "research_notes": "Geo music-affinity packs: what a market actually streams, from public sources — city/state Spotify chart analyses, Spotify's own research on place and musical identity, and the Nature study on cultural divergence in streaming. Empirical anchors: Kendrick Lamar ~10% of streaming in California cities and strong in Detroit/Portland/Phoenix but minimal in Memphis/Nashville where country dominates; local-genre loyalty is strongest where a distinctive regional style exists (country, regional mexican, funk carioca, afrobeats, grime). A pack MODULATES a demographic direction (genre boosts, style keywords, search modifiers) and carries the platform geo keys needed to actually buy that market. This is the hyperpersonalization layer: segment x geo -> a music brief no brand tunes by hand today.",
    "sources": [
      "https://bleumag.com/music/american-artists-rule-spotify-charts-at-home-and-abroad/",
      "https://www.skoove.com/blog/spotify-local-vs-global-music-us/",
      "https://www.skoove.com/blog/spotify-local-vs-global-music/",
      "https://research.atspotify.com/2019/07/environmental-changes-and-the-dynamics-of-musical-identity",
      "https://research.atspotify.com/2024/05/exploring-local-musics-place-in-global-streaming",
      "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41599-021-00855-1"
    ]
